  "spiritual_reading": "# Spiritual Translation\n\n** ¶1:** Wisdom, in the very origin of all things, existed in full ness. The Divine Word , which is the first proce eding of all understanding , concerned itself with the separation of what is true from what is false. The most elevated states of the mind were raised toward still higher states of perception , and these expanded until the conflict between good and evil should begin . The domin ion of wisdom existed in those elevated states, proce eding from all the successive un foldings of spiritual life — that wisdom which no fals ity has ever entered .\n\n**¶2:** Falsity and evil, which constitute the unre gen erate mind, had their origin deep within the natural will . They p oured forth from themselves ce aselessly. All that the merely natural man poss esses belongs to this realm of spiritual darkness . It is utt erly remote from wisdom .\n\n**¶3:** This is the first teaching concerning the eternal states: that good and evil each exist in their own nature; that they are divided from one another by their very essence , and have been so from et ernity. Yet fals ity and evil rose up against wisdom and good, des iring to reign over a spiritual substance that did not belong to them. Evil spread cont ention into what was peaceful ; it disturbed the order of spiritual life , and asc ended against it — and in this arose the great spiritual crisis .\n\n**¶4:** The Divine Power went forth from the Infinite — which is the Divine Human in His first proce eding. He cloth ed Himself in divine truths as in an armor of wisdom , and went to meet all the enmity of evil. He subd ued and fixed it upon its own nature , so that its power of agg ression was arrested by those very truths it had sought to destroy .\n\n**¶5:** He brought forth divine love as the ruling good of the spiritual world , and all the un fol dings of wisdom were illumin ated by it . The Divine proce eding as ordering Providence established the whole spiritual universe . The natural mind was set in place . Wisdom and fals ity, which from the beginning existed in their own n atures, were now distinguished and arranged , and the external truths by which the mind is cloth ed were given to each degree . He ordered the successive states of spiritual progression — the recurring cycles by which the inter iors of the mind are opened — and these were set in the highest places, so that they might govern all that is of fals ity and evil. The foundation of divine order was made firm, and every part of the arrangement was established.\n\n**¶6 :** Beneath the celest ial degree he set all lower things ; and above the natural mind he established three degrees of external reception , con joined one to another. He enclosed the natural mind within four elevated states of perception and three containing forms of truth, together with its general knowledges and its higher app rehensions — all set in order upon it. This whole spiritual arrangement stood firm as a restra int upon the powers of evil, binding them — for the good that had become ent angled with fals ity was now held within a structure capable of separ ating them .\n\n**¶7:** Then came the Divine proce eding in its third manner — as Re deemer. It purified all wisdom that had been obsc ured, by presenting the image of the Divine Human itself . It became the means of redem ption for all things.\n\n** ¶8:** All states of good and evil exist throughout the whole spiritual constitution of the human being . The fire of self-love blaz es within the natural mind, and it dev ours what surro unds it. But whatever is of genuine wisdom is also present there : it becomes the purifying agent, and when freed , it asc ends to the spiritual degree that is its true home . Conversely, whatever is of falsity and evil is drawn out and gathered together into a bond of con finement. The inter iors are unveiled ; all things of good enter into the Divine and become one with it — they become as the frag rance of worship — and the whole is established . Good and truth reign forever, and the one Divine comes to be known as sole sovereign over the whole of the mind , above every state within it. From that time on ward there is found no advers ary against the Father, who is the sovereign of all wisdom and all good .\n\n**¶9:** These are the states in which all spiritual things unf old, from the very beginning: good and evil, truth and falsity, are inter mingled and con joined with one another — and the entire work of regener ation is their separation .",
  "reconstructions": [
    {
      "paragraph": 1,
      "reconstructed_text": "(1) [The teaching of the] Light [is that] which he has unveiled [to (2) all of] his disciples [. The (3)] entire [mystery] of wisdom [and every] word in the beginning [he proclaimed] concerning the separation [of the Light from the Darkness. The aeons rose in] the heights [and ascended] to the heights [of the Light,] and they spread out [in their fullness. Then the Darkness rose up unt]il they should make war [against the] kingdom [of the L]ight [that abides] in the heights [f]rom all the aeons [of] the Light, the one that no [Darkness has ever entered] in it."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 2,
      "reconstructed_text": "[Below exists] the Darkness, the world [of evil, and] their root [is in the depth,] which poured forth [from itself ceaselessly.] the one that the earth has [brought forth from itself is of the] Darkness [entirely, and] it is far from the Light [of the heights.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 3,
      "reconstructed_text": "for each one of them exists [in its own nature, and] they are divided from one another by their [essence and their being] in an eternality since the [beginning of time.] (4) the Darkness has made war against the Light, desiring that it would reign over an essence not its own. It spread a quarrel [into the place of peace, and] it disturbed [the order of the Light. It] came up, it [set itself against the Light. And in this great] need."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 4,
      "reconstructed_text": "The power came forth from [the Father of Greatness, which] is [the Fir]st Man. He [clothed himself in] the armour of Light [and went forth against] all [the enmity]. He crucified it in [the depth of matter, and] the armour [of Light bound its power.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 5,
      "reconstructed_text": "[Then] he brought the sun [and the moon to illuminate] the Light aeons [in the heights. And the] Living Spirit spread out the universe [and established] the earth [beneath. He separated] the Light and the Darkness in the beginning [of the creation,] and the garments. He gave [them to every degree of the powers.] He set in order the [heavens and the firmaments] and the wheel of the course [of the stars] in the heights, that they would [govern every power] of the Darkness. He stood firm [and was f]ixed. He constructed the foundation [of the whole, and] all of it was set up."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 6,
      "reconstructed_text": "Underneath [the firmaments he placed] all of them; and also above he [set in place the thre]e earths, they being conjoined. He enclosed the earth in [the midst of f]our mountains and three vessels [, together with all that is] in its seas and its mountains [, all set in] order upon it. This universe stood firm [as] a bond for the evil powers [, restraining the li]ght that they joined with the Darkness [within this structure.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 7,
      "reconstructed_text": "Then the Third Ambassador! [He purified the Light] by his image. He became [redeemer of] all things."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 8,
      "reconstructed_text": "(5) [The powers of good and evil,] they are in all the [parts of the u]niverse, and the fire blazes in it, and it is devoured [by the fire. But] all [the substance] of the Light also, and he becomes purifier, and goes up to his essence. Conversely, the Darkness which is in [it is drawn] out, and it is gathered in to a bond [of confinement. The hidden things] unveil [themselves,] and they go in to him and become [as a sweet pe]rfume [. The whole is s]et up [in truth, an]d they reign for ever, and a single God comes to be [sovereign ov]er the totality, being above the totality. You find no opponent from this time on against the Father, the King of the Light and the [Lord of all wisdom and goodness.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 9,
      "reconstructed_text": "[These are the states in] which they occur in, from the beginning [of all things until their final separation:] they are mixed and joined with one another."
    }
